871 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\072\050\050A simpler particle system that launches red lines outward to grab the player\031s attention and to signal that the enemy is about to attack\056\050\050Description\072\050\050This is most likely done by using local space relative to the enemy who is attacking\054 and works by setting a constant velocity unaffected by gravity outward in a circle from the characters anchor point\056 Over the lifetime of the particle it fades out smoothly\056\n\050Use Case\072\050\050Proper particles for telegraphing an incoming attack is vital\054 and if done poorly could be too distracting\056\050\050Effectiveness\072\0505\0575\050Relevance to game studio\072\0505\0575 \055 Telegraphing attacks is critical in any fighting games)
     /K [ 21 ]
     /P 872 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

872 0 obj
  << /K [ 20 871 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

873 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\072\050The orbs flight trail is a perfect example of a good use of particle systems for information\056 As it flies and the trail exists a player can subconsciously extrapolate it\031s trajectory from the visible trail\056\050Description\072\050\050This particle system is a classic trail style system which works in world space and just leaves particles that dissipate after a short time\056 These particles don\031t have any velocity and are static to function as a trail properly\056\n\050Use Case\072\050\050Critical for any multi axis projectiles\054 or players may find these enemies extremely frustrating to deal with\056\050\050Effectiveness\072\0505\0575\050Relevance to game studio\072\0504\0575 \055 We will most likely be creating a ranged enemy so trails will be important\056)
     /K [ 23 ]
     /P 874 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

874 0 obj
  << /K [ 22 873 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

875 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\072\050\050The explosion of the orb that is launched at the player\056 Once again a very effective use of particles to convey information to the player\054 in this case we are effectively showing the range of the explosion as well as how quickly it falls off from the center\054 which is conveyed by the intensity\056\050\050Description\072\050\050The explosion is most likely done in world space originating from the anchor point of the orb when it explodes\056 I would hazard a guess that it is made up of quite a few components\054 as you can clearly see the energy pulsating from it initially when it lands\054 then the main spherical explosion and lastly the little shrapnel particles that shoot out\056\n\050Use Case\072\050\nThis showcases effective use of visuals to convey timing\054 and lethality\056 This would be best used for any timer based weapons or explosions\056 \n\050Effectiveness\072\0505\0575\050Relevance to game studio\072\0503\0575 \055 Depending on if we have timer based weapons or projectiles concepts here could be utilized\056)
     /K [ 25 ]
     /P 876 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

876 0 obj
  << /K [ 24 875 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

877 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\072\050\050This is a weapon that you can unlock that has a stun affect on enemies and creates a whip\055like affect in a 2d space\056\050\050Description\072\050\050Most likely this is made by generating an endpoint for the whip to land at and then calculating multiple points above and below that point on the way in order to get a random lightning chain like effect\054 this is in world space as it does not move with the character\056\n\050Use Case\072\050\nThis is a great example of how the visuals should change to match the item and how making things look cooler\054 can result in them feeling stronger\056\n\050Effectiveness\072\0503\0575\050Relevance to game studio\072\0501\0575 \055 Our weapons should be very simple but if we have extra time to add variations\054 we may want to consider\056)
     /K [ 27 ]
     /P 878 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

