909 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Ice Bomb\n\nParticles spawn in a circular form around the explosion point of the bomb\056 Particles then fall and collide with any floor terrain\054 while some do not creating an impactful explosion\n\nCreated with the local space of the bomb\054 the particles spawn a set radius distance away from the origin point of the bomb\056 Multiple instances of the article is spawned in a 360\260 space around the origin point\056 After a random time between a certain time range \050i\056e 0\0565\0551s\051 the particles fall and collide with terrain or fall continuosly downwards\056 If colliding with terrain\054 it will then fall through after another random time range \050i\056e 0\0565\0551s\051\056\050\050Useful for finding samples to look at when designing projectile  particle slides\056)
     /K [ 59 ]
     /P 910 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

910 0 obj
  << /K [ 58 909 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

911 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Distortion Effect on Portal\n\nDistortion visual effects around the warp portal that distorts the background that it is in front of\056 Creates the feeling of a powerful otherworldly phenomenon\056\050\050Potentially created using a distortion effect available within the game engine\031s particle system\054 shaders and math equations\056 Appears to emanate from the center of the portal in a circular pattern\056 \050\050While the portal itself is not useful\054 the distortion effect can be useful for showcasing heat in the environment\054 or to enhance shockwave attacks\056 Adding more game feel to mechanics\056)
     /K [ 61 ]
     /P 912 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

912 0 obj
  << /K [ 60 911 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

913 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Leave visible on foreground\n\nLeaves that visibly fall in front of all traversable terrain as compared to the background that is mostly a still image\056 Evokes the different layers of the map\054 adding detail and depth to an otherwise 2D game\056\n\nCreated in the world space\054 similar to a filter on the camera of the game\056 The leaves fall from top right moving downwards to the left\054 a set velocity to match how the player is constantly traversing to the right during gameplay\056\n\nPossibly being used within our game to create more environmental details\054 and make the world feel more alive\056)
     /K [ 63 ]
     /P 914 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

914 0 obj
  << /K [ 62 913 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

915 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\050Communication Goal\072 Tells the player that the door has been broken\054 and will no \050longer act as a barrier in the environment\056\n\050Description\072 Also appears to be sprite\055based\056 After the first frame\054 the door sprite \050is swapped out with a sideways\055facing\054 broken door sprite\056 The flash of light from \050the weapon contacting the door splits and then dissipates\056 The chunks of door are \050particles that fade quickly and follow a scripted path\056\n\nUse Case\072 We can adopt a similar effect for breaking of environmental obstacles\072 doors\054\050crates\054 sewer grates\056\050\nEffectiveness\072 5\0575\056 Clear\054 visually expressive and powerful\056\n\nRelevance\072 5\0575\056 On top of the above example\054 we could also use this effect for the \050destruction of enemies\054 since they are robots and we will need to show them being\050\035scrapped\035\056)
     /K [ 65 ]
     /P 916 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

916 0 obj
  << /K [ 64 915 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

917 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\050Communication Goal\072 Feedback that the bomb is traveling along a certain arc\054 \050and a blinking effect to signal that it will soon explode\054 and finally an area\050affected by damage from the bomb\056\n\050Description\072 While the bomb itself is a sprite\054 it has a particle effect for the trail\056 \050The particles of the trail are distributed along an arc\054 with a slight offset so that\050the line does not appear perfect\056 These particles fade over time through an \050\035alpha over lifetime\035 setting\056\n\nUse Case\072 At this time\054 we do not have any enemies that shoot an arcing projectile\056\n\nEffectiveness\072 5\0575\056 Clear and concise\054 colors stand out against the environment\056\n\nRelevance\072 1\0575\056We do not have any enemy variants to apply this to\056)
     /K [ 67 ]
     /P 918 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

918 0 obj
  << /K [ 66 917 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

919 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\050Communication Goal\072 Feedback that the player has pressed \050the jump button while airborne\056\n\050Description\072 Appears to be a sprite\055based particle\056 Starts at the base\050of the bottom foot when activated\054 stays in world space as the player\050moves upwards\056 Simple visual\054 sprite is changed over lifetime but no \050behavior or color changes\056\n\nUse Case\072 We could use a similar simple effect for our double jump\056\n\nEffectiveness\072 4\0575\056 Simple visuals provide immediate feedback after\050a button press\054 lacks visual flair\056\n\nRelevance\072 5\0575\056 We have a double jump\054 copying this exactly would \050convey what we need to the player\056)
     /K [ 69 ]
     /P 920 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

920 0 obj
  << /K [ 68 919 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

921 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\050Communication Goal\072 Feedback that the player has pressed \034down\035 while airborne\056 Gives a \050sense of forceful and quick movement\056\n\050Description\072 This effect has three parts\072 the \034shadow clones\035\054 the rubble\054 and the dust cloud\056\nThe shadow clones are always present when moving and jumping\054 and fade after a short time\056\050When performing a ground slam\054 they become more opaque and saturated\054 highlighting how\050quickly the player is moving\056 This is further backed up by the rubble and dust cloud\056 The rubble\050is sprite based and interacts with the environment\054 tumbling along the floor or bouncing off a wall\050before fading\056 The dust cloud is static in world space where the player landed\054 and does not interact \050with the environment\056\n\nUse Case\072 We won\031t have a true ground slam\054 but we can use a similar idea for when our player lands\050after a jump\056\n\nEffectiveness\072 5\0575\056 Sells the feeling of powerfully impacting the ground\056\n\nRelevance\072 3\0575\056 Our player is a normal human being\054 and not in a fantasy environment\054 so they can\031t\050take as much of a fall\056 We could have a less\055powerful version of this\054 relying more on the shadow clone\050and dust cloud parts of the effect rather than the rubble\056)
     /K [ 71 ]
     /P 922 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

922 0 obj
  << /K [ 70 921 0 R ]
     /P 965 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

923 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Summary\050Communication Goal\072 Feedback that the enemy has been damaged\054 and that their action\057attack has\050been interrupted\056\n\050Description\072 The main part of the effect is the blood splatter\056 When the enemy is hit\054 the splatter particles\050are spawned at a pre\055defined location on the enemy on whichever side has been hit\054 not at specific impact\050point\056 The splatter has a scripted path\054 the velocity or trajectory is not affected by the \050power of the player\031s attack\056 Particles do not interact with the player\054 but do splatter onto the ground briefly \050before fading\056\n\nUse Case\072 Our enemies are robots and will splatter oil when damaged\054 but otherwise than the color swap\050we can pretty much use this exactly\056 \n\nEffectiveness\072 4\0575\056 You can easily tell that the enemy has been damaged\054 although some variation in the \050effect would be interesting\056\n\nRelevance\072 5\0575\056 This could be used as\055is\056 It would be neat to have the oil splatter onto the player character\056)
     /K [ 73 ]
     /P 924 0 R
     /Pg 850 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

